From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:47:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH alpha 3/4] winedmo: Use destroy parameters for WOW64 demuxer
 teardown

wow64_demuxer_destroy() passes its local object to demuxer_destroy(), which interprets it as struct demuxer_destroy_params. Using the larger create structure places the demuxer handle at a different offset, so the 64-bit Unix side can read the wrong handle during 32-bit media teardown.

Use the matching destroy structure and initialize it before marshalling.
---
 dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c b/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
index 657e498..dc4b7be 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@ static NTSTATUS wow64_demuxer_destroy( void *arg )
         struct winedmo_demuxer demuxer;
         PTR32 context;
     } *params32 = arg;
-    struct demuxer_create_params params;
+    struct demuxer_destroy_params params = {0};
     NTSTATUS status;
 
     params.demuxer = params32->demuxer;
